Subject: [PATCH 2/3] zib: Patch review workflow - Archiving mail
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Change-Id: lknvxszrtysqspqrwnmmurkkkzmzwutt

Archiving closes a message for everyone by moving its file into
maildir/archive/, so the workflow must allow that move. Two rules in
the document forbade it: the moderator accepted commits that only add
messages, and a message's file was never to be renamed. Followed as
written, they would reject every archive commit.

The file still keeps its content and name, and only its directory
changes, so the list stays immutable in the sense that matters: no
message is ever edited.
---
