 zib/patch-review-workflow.org | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/zib/patch-review-workflow.org b/zib/patch-review-workflow.org
index 3914398..ef892ed 100644
--- a/zib/patch-review-workflow.org
+++ b/zib/patch-review-workflow.org
@@ -80,7 +80,8 @@ Developing new work:
   =submissions= repo
 ** Moderator
 - Fetch devlist commits from =submissions= repo
-- Verify that the commits only add maildir messages and make no other
+- Verify that the commits only add maildir messages, or move existing
+  ones unchanged into or out of =maildir/archive/=, and make no other
   changes.
 - Decide which messages to cherry-pick or reject
 - Cherry-pick commits to =mail= branch
@@ -104,7 +105,9 @@ at this point.
 ** maildir doesn't rename files
 notmuch by default renames files to indicate if they've been
 seen. This will be disabled by setting =maildir.synchronize_flags
-false=. Once a message is added to the list, it does not get renamed.
+false=. Once a message is added to the list, its file is never renamed
+or edited. The one exception is archiving, which moves the file
+unchanged in and out of =maildir/archive/=.
 ** maintainer can post directly to the list
 Trusted members don't have a moderation queue.
 * Contributor workspace setup
@@ -157,10 +160,28 @@ The rules are simple:
   is tagged with ~inbox~
 - any email from someone else, that user has directly replied to, is
   tagged with ~replied~, and the inbox tag is removed
+- any email under =maildir/archive/= is tagged with ~archived~, and the
+  inbox tag is removed
 
 ~just index~ in the =mail= jj workspace runs =notmuch new=, which
 applies the tags that it can and does whatever post-processing it
 needs.
+
+Archiving closes a message that needs no answer, e.g. a patch applied
+without a reply, or a question already settled. Anyone may archive a
+message by moving its file unchanged from =maildir/cur/= to
+=maildir/archive/cur/= and committing the move like any other mail. It
+is archived for everyone. Moving it back unarchives it. Archiving works
+per message, not per thread, so a later message in the same thread
+still lands in the inbox.
+
+In the =mail= jj workspace:
+
+#+BEGIN_SRC sh
+f=$(notmuch search --output=files id:<message-id>)
+mkdir -p maildir/archive/cur
+mv "${f}" maildir/archive/cur/
+#+END_SRC
 * Shared repo setup
 Two repos shared across jails:
 - =/jails/share/lab.git= owned by host user =patmaddox=
